WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:07.020
After 17 years, two of the most recognizable
X-Men in the movie world — Hugh Jackman's

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:12.250
Wolverine and Patrick Stewart's Professor
Charles Xavier — have given their final

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.870
bows as their beloved characters.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:19.920
Logan may be the most dystopian X-film, but
it also represents a new beginning, introducing

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.240
a brand new character — Laura Kinney — played
by Dafne Keen.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.580
But what do we know about this fresh mutant
hero and the young actress who portrays her?

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.910
Who is Laura Kinney?

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:37.740
Very simply put, Laura is a clone of Wolverine
made by the Transigen Corporation, engineered

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.380
to do everything her genetic poppa can do.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.910
Which is legitimately terrifying.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:44.080
"No.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.250
No.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.420
No."

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:50.790
She shares Logan's superior strength, agility,
and mutant healing abilities.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:55.640
She's also been given dual adamantium claws
on each hand, and has the added bonus of a

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.820
deadly claw on each foot.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:02.700
In every sense but gender, she's Wolverine
Junior, and her on-screen story closely mirrors

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.320
her comic book origins.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.940
Writer Craig Kyle first created X-23 during
the four-year run of the Warner Bros animated

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.480
series X-Men: Evolution.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:17.290
Laura Kinney rapidly cut a swath of popularity
through the superhero world, getting reverse-adapted

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:22.870
back into Marvel Comics, and landing two miniseries
and an ongoing solo series.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:29.440
Like Wolverine, X-23 was one of the X-Men's
most successful upstarts, and also like Wolverine,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:35.480
she's done time on several superhero squads,
including the hyper-violent X-Force, the All-New

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.510
X-Men, and the Avengers Academy comic series.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:43.610
Eventually, Laura was officially dubbed as
the "All-New Wolverine" when the Marvel Universe

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:49.510
rebooted in 2016, a title she's carried since,
as of the making of this video.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:54.400
So it wouldn't be unrealistic to expect the
movies to follow suit.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.970
Who is Dafne Keen?

00:01:55.970 --> 00:02:01.950
Born in 2005, Dafne Keen Fernandez is the
child of a British father and a Spanish mother.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:07.180
As a result, she's bilingual — one of the
requirements for the role, since James Mangold

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.240
envisioned a Hispanic X-23.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:15.140
She's also well-versed in gymnastics and martial
arts, which were obviously also important

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:19.660
for the role of a girl who literally kills
dozens of people with her floor routine.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:24.420
Her mother is Spanish actress and playwright
Maria Fernandez Ache, and her father is actor

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:30.050
Will Keen, both of whom have acted extensively
for theater, film, and television in Spain

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:31.050
and the U.K.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:36.200
Most recently, Mr. Keen landed a prominent
recurring role as Michael Adeane in the Netflix

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.370
biographical drama The Crown.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:43.800
Will Keen has also appeared on the longtime
1940s-era mystery series Foyle's War and the

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:48.099
TV series The Refugees, in which he co-starred
with his daughter.

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:50.040
How'd she get the role?

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:55.070
In Logan, Dafne Keen's characterizations and
feral intensity were leaps and bounds beyond

00:02:55.070 --> 00:03:00.020
most child actors, immediately catching the
attention of director James Mangold.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:04.660
According to Mangold, her audition tape included
moments where the young actress clambered

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.810
up bookshelves, prowling and tumbling around
her parent's house.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.680
After watching her run through a few scenes,
the director was mesmerized enough by her

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.810
performance to immediately request a screen
test.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:16.810
And he admitted:

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:20.420
"The biggest question to me, was will you
believe that this little girl is capable of

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:22.900
doing what the comics have proposed she can
do?

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:28.170
I think in many ways, that's Dafne's amazing
achievement … holding it all together."

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:33.760
In a role as physically and emotionally demanding
as X-23, Keen was more than capable of bringing

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:39.010
the rage-filled mutant to life, even without
speaking for most of the movie.

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:43.020
Unbelievably, this was only her second time
on-screen.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.739
Will X-23 return?

00:03:44.739 --> 00:03:50.520
Hugh Jackman decided to step away from his
17-year run as the metal-boned mutant, so

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:56.330
a similarly named sequel is extremely unlikely,
despite the amazing success of Logan.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.340
But that doesn't mean X-23 won't reappear.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:03.450
Recently, Keen and director James Mangold
were both asked about their interest in the

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.849
continuing saga of Laura Kinney.

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:12.110
Mangold says he's "wide open to" the concept
of more X-23, and the young starlet likewise

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.480
sounds interested in pursuing the role as
well.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.239
Keen explained her relationship with the character,
telling The Hollywood Reporter,

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:22.749
"...she's complicated — she tries to be
so strong but she feels so vulnerable at the

00:04:22.749 --> 00:04:23.749
same time.

00:04:23.749 --> 00:04:24.949
I really love her.

00:04:24.949 --> 00:04:26.620
I'd love to keep playing her."

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:31.490
Of course, who wouldn't love to have a starring
role in a comic book movie franchise, especially

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:32.680
at the age of 12?

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:39.801
Fox's X-Men producer-slash-writer Simon Kinberg
already admitted an X-23 solo movie is a very

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:44.870
"real possibility," but at this time, the
studio hasn't finalized any plans for a follow-up.

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:50.139
The explosive success of the final Wolverine
outing will undoubtedly light up all sorts

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:54.509
of new possibilities for the future of the
franchise, and there's no way they're leaving

00:04:54.509 --> 00:04:56.979
the All-New Wolverine out of the action.

00:04:56.979 --> 00:04:57.999
Thanks for watching!

00:04:57.999 --> 00:05:00.770
